 "teaches": [
  "replies puts quick-reply chips in a scrolling row above the composer; a tap sends one host action (reply) with the chip's index, so the app answers as if it had been typed",
  "A bot is just theirs: one lead Avatar on its last message, a typing line while it answers; attachment shows a card (the invoice) in the bubble",
  "RemoteCompose has no text input: the field asks the app for input (compose) and the app's draft can be shown back with draft (\"@draft\", a host text variable)"
 ],
